{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KmMX3qRdZRRRNX6ZANk48Z","type":"tool_result","content":"# US Farmers Markets by State - Total Summary\n\nBased on the data provided, here are the farmers markets (excluding territories):\n\nThe data shows farmers market counts across all 50 US states plus DC. The state with the highest count is California with 647, followed by New York with 555 and Pennsylvania with 426.\n\n**Total farmers markets across all US states and DC: 12,086**\n\nThis figure includes all 50 states and the District of Columbia, but excludes Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands as requested.\n\nThe data reveals significant regional variation, with larger agricultural states and those in the Northeast generally operating more farmers markets than smaller or less agriculturally-focused regions."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52434aed-1c04-4e7e-a9a0-38d1ad2df28e","uuid":"b71ddc35-99bd-4a57-9d22-dbd3029de946","timestamp":"2026-08-16T20:09:07.806Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":2651,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# US Farmers Markets by State - Total Summary\n\nBased on the data provided, here are the farmers markets (excluding territories):\n\nThe data shows farmers market counts across all 50 US states plus DC. The state with the highest count is California with 647, followed by New York with 555 and Pennsylvania with 426.\n\n**Total farmers markets across all US states and DC: 12,086**\n\nThis figure includes all 50 states and the District of Columbia, but excludes Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands as requested.\n\nThe data reveals significant regional variation, with larger agricultural states and those in the Northeast generally operating more farmers markets than smaller or less agriculturally-focused regions.","durationMs":2381,"url":"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv"}}
